## Review finding: no existing test rendered a genuinely asymmetric partial
## sphere's image. transforms.rib's Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360 is a full sphere
## (zmin = -radius, zmax = radius) and proves nothing about the zmin/zmax
## parameterization phase 3 fixed in GMANSphere::getLocation. This one --
## zmin = -0.5, zmax = radius = 1 -- is the exact case the phase-3 prompt
## named, and asymmetric: a cap is missing, a hemisphere is not.
##
## Explicit Clipping, not the RI_EPSILON-near default: this shape hits a
## general near-clip precision defect (see AGENTS.md's "Near-clip precision
## at the default Clipping"), same as a camera-facing Disk.
Display "partial_sphere.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
	LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
	Sides 1
	Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
	Sphere 1 -0.5 1 360
WorldEnd
